## 4. Step-by-Step Build Order

We build in **vertical slices** — each step produces something you can actually see and use.

---

### Step 1: FastAPI Project Skeleton + Database Connection
**Goal**: A running backend that can talk to your local PostgreSQL.

What we build:
- FastAPI project with proper folder structure (`app/`, `models/`, `schemas/`, `routers/`)
- SQLAlchemy models that mirror your existing 14 tables (NOT recreating them — just mapping to what exists)
- A single health-check endpoint: `GET /api/health` → returns `{ "status": "ok", "db": "connected" }`
- Environment config via `.env` file (DB password stays local, never committed)

**Security baked in from Day 1**:
- `.env` in `.gitignore`
- CORS middleware configured
- Input validation via Pydantic on every endpoint

**What you'll see**: Hit `http://localhost:8000/docs` and get a full interactive Swagger UI.

---

### Step 2: Authentication System (Registration + Login + JWT)
**Goal**: Users can register, log in, and get a secure token.

What we build:
- `POST /api/auth/register` — Creates investor, hashes password with bcrypt
- `POST /api/auth/login` — Validates credentials, returns JWT access token (15 min expiry) + refresh token (7 day, HttpOnly cookie)
- `POST /api/auth/refresh` — Issues new access token from refresh token
- `GET /api/auth/me` — Returns current user profile (protected route)
- Dependency injection: `get_current_user()` extracts and validates JWT on every protected endpoint

**Security maxxing**:
- Passwords hashed with bcrypt (your DB already has `PASSWORD_HASH` column)
- Short-lived access tokens (15 min)
- Refresh tokens in HttpOnly cookies (JavaScript can't steal them)
- Every protected route requires valid JWT — no exceptions

---

### Step 3: Core Portfolio & Trading API Endpoints
**Goal**: The API can do everything a trading app needs.

What we build (wrapping your existing SQL/views):
- `GET /api/portfolio` → Queries `v_portfolio_summary` for the logged-in user
- `GET /api/orders` → Queries `v_order_with_trade` with pagination
- `POST /api/orders` → Inserts into `ORDER_RECORD` (your `trg_validate_order` trigger handles validation!)
- `DELETE /api/orders/{id}` → Cancels an order (your `trg_order_prevent_cancel_executed` trigger blocks invalid cancels!)
- `GET /api/securities` → List/search securities with `ILIKE` (your query #2 from application queries)
- `GET /api/fund-transactions` → Queries `v_fund_ledger`
- `POST /api/fund-transactions` → Deposit/withdraw (your `trg_fund_txn_update_balance` trigger auto-updates balance!)
- `GET /api/brokers/performance` → Queries `v_broker_performance`

> [!NOTE]
> Notice how most of the heavy lifting is done by your existing triggers and views. The API is mostly a thin, secure layer on top.

**Security maxxing**:
- Every endpoint filters by `investor_id` from the JWT — users can NEVER see another user's data
- Rate limiting with `slowapi` (in-memory, no Redis needed yet)
- Input validation on every request body

---

### Step 4: Next.js Frontend — The Dashboard
**Goal**: A stunning, dark-mode portfolio dashboard running on `localhost:3000`.

What we build:
- Login / Registration pages
- **Dashboard** with cards showing: Total Portfolio Value, Today's P&L, Number of Holdings
- **Portfolio Table** showing each holding with unrealized P&L (green/red color coding)
- **Order History** with status badges (OPEN, EXECUTED, CANCELLED)
- **Place Order** form (select security, order type, quantity)
- **Fund Management** page (deposit/withdraw)
- **Broker Performance** charts

**Design**: Dark theme, glassmorphism cards, smooth transitions, responsive layout. Think Zerodha Kite meets Robinhood.

---

### Step 5: LangChain + Ollama — AI Portfolio Assistant (Free, Local)
**Goal**: A chat interface where users ask questions about their portfolio in plain English.

What we build:
- Install **Ollama** locally → download a model like `llama3.1:8b` (runs on CPU, ~4GB RAM)
- LangChain SQL Agent connected to your PostgreSQL database
- Chat endpoint: `POST /api/chat` → User sends a message, LangChain converts it to SQL, runs it, returns a human-readable answer
- Example queries the AI can handle:
  - *"What's my best performing stock?"*
  - *"How much have I invested in mutual funds?"*
  - *"Show me all orders I placed last week"*
  - *"Which broker has the lowest commission rate?"*

**Security maxxing**:
- The LangChain agent uses a **read-only** database connection (separate from the main API)
- SQL queries generated by the LLM are validated and sandboxed — no `DROP`, `DELETE`, or `UPDATE` allowed
- The agent can only access data for the logged-in user's `investor_id`

---

### Step 6 (Future): LangGraph — Autonomous Agent Workflows
**Goal**: Multi-step AI agents that can take action.

This is the advanced step you add once everything else is stable:
- **Portfolio Advisor**: Analyzes holdings → fetches market data → suggests rebalancing
- **Conditional Order Agent**: *"Buy AAPL if it drops below 150"* → monitors and executes
- **Report Generator**: Generates monthly portfolio reports as PDFs

