## 5. When to Think About Cloud (Later)

Only after you have a fully working local app:

| Service | Free Tier Option |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Database hosting** | Supabase (500MB free), Neon (0.5GB free), or Railway |
| **Backend hosting** | Railway (free tier), Render (free tier), or Fly.io |
| **Frontend hosting** | Vercel (free for personal projects — perfect for Next.js) |
| **AI API (if needed)** | Google Gemini API (free tier: 15 RPM), Groq (free tier) |

> [!TIP]
> Vercel + Supabase + Railway free tiers are more than enough to host a portfolio project for interviews and demos. Total cost: **$0**.

---

## 6. Recommended Build Order Summary

```
Step 1: FastAPI + DB Connection        ← Foundation (1-2 days)
Step 2: Auth (JWT + bcrypt)            ← Security core (1-2 days)  
Step 3: Portfolio & Trading Endpoints  ← Core features (2-3 days)
Step 4: Next.js Frontend Dashboard     ← Visual wow factor (3-5 days)
Step 5: LangChain + Ollama Chat        ← AI differentiator (2-3 days)
Step 6: LangGraph Agents               ← Advanced showcase (3-5 days)
───────────────────────────────────────
Cloud deployment                       ← Only when ready to share
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Each step produces a **working, demo-able product**. You don't need to finish all 6 steps to have something impressive. Even Steps 1-3 alone give you a secure, production-grade REST API backed by a properly designed database — that's already a strong portfolio project.
